UID:stanford_campus-localist-53878610973590-53878610983838@local-events
DESCRIPTION:The East Asia Library at Stanford University will host a print
  exhibition by Kim Bong-Jun\, a leading figure in Korean Minjung (People
 ’s) Art\, from September 29 to December 11\, 2026. Active since the 1980
 s\, Kim has developed a distinctive visual language that combines traditio
 nal Korean folk art and popular expression with contemporary art\, reflect
 ing the lives and realities of ordinary people and envisioning possibiliti
 es for a more just and ecological future. The exhibition explores Kim’s 
 conce\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-10-02 11:14 PDT
LOCATION:Lathrop Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Cantor Arts] Solid Pictures: Photosculpture and the Making of Mod
 ern Likeness
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261006
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261006
DTSTAMP:20261002T181401Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-52881097589713-52881097603045@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Before 3D printing\, there was photosculpture. Curated by Patr
 ick R. Crowley\, Associate Curator of European Art\, Solid Pictures is the
  first major exhibition to explore these largely overlooked objects first 
 conceived in 1859 by the twenty-nine-year-old French artist and inventor F
 rançois Willème. Employing projection technologies and mechanical instru
 ments\, Willème and his team of operators translated photographic negativ
 es into solid figures across a variety of media\, aiming to create afforda
 bl\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://museum.stanford.edu/exhibitions/soli
 d-pictures\nLast synced: 2026-10-02 11:14 PDT
LOCATION:Cantor Arts Center
URL:https://museum.stanford.edu/exhibitions/solid-pictures
END:VEVENT
